    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Cal Raleigh** stands as our premier offensive anchor with a 77.68 efficiency score. His matchup against Sugano (4.91 xERA) is the most favorable on the board, and the combination of a park factor boost and a prime cleanup spot makes him a must-start. Joining him in the top tier are **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.56) and **Bryce Harper** (65.78). **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a rare situational boost due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which increases his stolen base upside, while **Bryce Harper** remains our highest floor play, supported by a rock-solid .383 xwOBA that mitigates the slight park disadvantage at his venue. \n\nWe have identified distinct platoon and matchup advantages elsewhere: **JJ Bleday** (65.61) is a strong play against the lefty Peterson, as his dynamic platoon profile provides a significant boost, and **Dylan Beavers** (56.73) earns his spot in the lineup specifically because he avoids the gauntlet of elite arms, facing Misiorowski (2.32 xERA) while leveraging a park-driven efficiency surge. Conversely, the benching of **Jung Hoo Lee** (39.91) represents our most difficult personnel decision. He fell just short of our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor due to a negative platoon split against the lefty Dreyer and a high-caliber opposing arm, forcing us to prioritize the raw efficiency of players like **Justin Crawford**, whose speed profile remains a strategic necessity despite his low batting order.\n\nRisk management is paramount today, particularly regarding the high-end talent facing top-tier arms. **Zack Gelof** (40.16) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (49.20) are both dancing on the edge of our efficiency floor due to their matchups against Williams and Misiorowski, respectively. We are absorbing the risk of these elite arms to maintain our desired volume of stolen base threats, but these slots are on \"short notice\" should a late lineup change occur. While **Tyler Freeman** remains relegated to the minors and **Matt Chapman** is unavailable due to his IL stint, we remain satisfied with the current deployment of our healthy depth, ensuring we stay aggressive in the counting categories as the season winds down.",
